# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   Indicate which Python version your project is compiled against:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if the platform is not the same, the lock file might be different.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock contains the exact dependency version.
#   It is recommended to check this in to Git.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock contains the exact dependency version.
#   It is recommended to check this in to Git.
# pdm.lock

# virtualenv
#   It is not recommended to check in virtual environments.
#   It's better to recreate them as needed.
